---
title: Sharing
description: How access to your data is granted, shared with other people, and revoked.
---

Access to data is controlled by **grants** on nodes. A grant gives a person or an app a role
on a node and everything below it, together with the key needed to read it.

## Roles

- **read** can read the node and its subtree.
- **write** can also change them.
- **admin** can also change who has access.

An app's role is also limited by the scopes you approved for it, such as `calendar:read`.

## Sharing with people

Share a node with another NeoWorks user, and their devices receive its key sealed to their
public identity. Sharing can cover a whole calendar or a single item, and some data can be
shared in part, for example only when you are free or busy.

## Link shares

A link share lets anyone with the link open a node. The key is part of the link after the
`#`, so it is never sent to the server.

## Revoking

Revoking a grant removes the server's willingness to serve the data. The affected node keys
are rotated the next time you open the account vault, so a revoked key stops protecting new
data.

## Audit

Grants and revocations are written to a signed access log.
